[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) is marked **known: one issue, one fix queued**. The reports in it
describe three different bugs. The queued parser fix closes only the first one. Each bug now has a
ticket of its own, and the counts below come from the merged reports at render time.

<Callout kind="warn">
Do not close #4471 when the parser fix ships. The booking-v3 form and the one-day moves will keep
coming in, and both need their own fixes.
</Callout>

## What #4471 holds

<CauseTable ticket={4471} {filed} />

## The three bugs

- **`parser`: the shared parser reads dates month first** ([ticket]({filed.parser})). Our tenants
  write the day first, so day and month swap. It covers app and email reports from every tenant, and
  form reports from booking-v2 tenants, whose hint already says `DD/MM/YYYY`.
- **`hint`: booking-v3 asks for month first and reads day first** ([ticket]({filed.hint})). The form
  prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field. People type what it says, and the form reads the
  tenant's way. These are form reports from booking-v3 tenants only. The parser fix does not touch
  them.
- **`shift`: the date moves by one day** ([ticket]({filed.shift})). Day and month are not swapped.
  Lisbon gets Tuesday and Toronto gets Monday, "only June" is off, and an invite arrives before the
  booking. That is a time-zone or daylight-saving bug. The desk already noted these reports as a
  one-day move (`desk-notes.json`). Until now the table filed them under `parser` by tenant.

## How the split was made

- One id, one report: the export pages overlap, so repeated rows are dropped first.
- The cause comes from the tenant (its locale and booking form, `locales.ts`), never from intake's tag.
  Intake guesses from the reporter's browser. The `tagged as` column shows how often that guess is
  wrong.
- A report the desk read as a one-day move is `shift`, whatever its tenant.

## For the desk

- Triage by subject ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)) merged all three bugs
  because the reports share subject lines. Before you merge into a big ticket, check the cause with
  the [dedupe explorer](/kb/triage/dedupe).
- New date reports: file `hint` under the booking-v3 ticket, `shift` under the time-zone ticket, and
  the rest under #4471.

